+    # ready_for_review when marked ready — and fork PRs, which get no OIDC
+    # token so the run would die at startup on id-token: write; the
+    # same-repo check below is an ergonomic skip, not a security
+    # boundary), or on a PR comment containing
     # @review — or an @review comment on an External-labeled proxy ISSUE, which
     # reviews the tracked upstream PR and posts findings on the proxy (external
     # mode; see the reusable workflow). An explicit @review still works on a
diff --git a/.github/workflows/claude-review.yml b/.github/workflows/claude-review.yml
index fecefc1..cca28f8 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/claude-review.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/claude-review.yml
@@ -4,17 +4,20 @@ name: Claude review (reusable)
